---
description: Sweep a finding's whole family, then fix every instance. No severity tiers.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Review

No 应改 / 可改. Quality is one bar. Wrong output, drift, dead code, leftovers, inconsistent flags, empty shells, and nits are all findings. When reviewing, list the family and fix every instance in the same turn. Do not stop at a report.

A finding is a seed, not the report. Search the whole family before writing it down. The list must be every instance, not a sample.

Sweep by invariant, not by the file in view. For each finding, grep siblings before listing:

- Tables that can drift (edition names, 篇, axes, legal PDFs)
- Dead exports, unused params, leftover attributes
- HTML tags or UI copy built in TypeScript
- Empty 校记 / 今译 / 按语 still emitting a headed section
- Print pages carrying web-only attrs or a second script
- The same fact in workflow, README, and docs (branch, Source, command lists)

If that family was already swept, do not re-report the next sibling next round. That means the last review was incomplete.

After every edit, re-sweep the family before calling the review done. Re-reading only the last hunk is incomplete.

Before a design with tradeoffs, write the invariants. If they conflict, pick one set. Do not satisfy the last comment by adding a knob (`if` plus `on`, extra dispatch, tighter permissions than the official template). Prefer the smallest official recipe that meets the invariants.

Do not invent work. "The next union could also be derived" is not a finding. That ban does not excuse skipping the sibling grep.
